  "findings": [
    "The designed linker clears the TERT surface: minimum PAPAP heavy-atom clearance 8.22 A, 0 atoms below 2.5 A. So the graft is sterically compatible with binding 7TRE's TERT, and P12's 'a score would be fabricated' is wrong for the geometric part: the geometry is measurable and it passes.",
    "The epitope is charge-dominated, not shape-dominated. Of the 14 native residues, 6 are charged and they carry net -4. E168, E169, E171 and E215 contribute their carboxylates directly; E170 is the only positive residue in the patch and it does not touch TERT (6.66 A).",
    "The TERT surface the graft faces is net +1 within 5 A and changes sign with cutoff (+4 at 8 A): it is a mosaic of 6 basic and 2 acidic residues over a short range, which a rigidly negative peptide cannot match by charge alone. The negative graft is complementary to K78 and R132 specifically, not to the surface in aggregate.",
    "A straight C(172)-N(209) path (16.31 A) clears TERT by 7.96 A with 0.0% of its length below 3 A. Only 2 of the 36 deleted residues were at the interface, so the linker is not replacing a binding element - it is replacing a tether."
  ],
  "design_linker": "PAPAP",
  "verdict": {
    "sterically_compatible": true,
    "affinity_measured": false,
    "what_is_refuted": null,
    "what_is_established": "geometric compatibility with the deposited TERT surface",
    "what_remains": "any affinity, any on-rate, any competition - an experiment"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Rigid body. TERT and the 14 native residues are held where the crystal put them; only the 5-residue linker moved. Real binding needs both sides to adjust.",
    "7TRE is 8.0 atoms/residue, so TERT is represented to CB for many residues. Every clearance is against modelled atoms and is an UPPER bound on the true clearance.",
    "No staple. The WP48 design is stapled at W167-L211; the staple cannot be built offline (needs files.rcsb.org), so the construct measured here is the unstapled peptide.",
    "No solvent, no entropy, no electrostatics. This is a collision test plus a composition count, not a score."
  ],
